    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0609" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2173: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1919-04-10T19:40:00-04:00"
                            notBefore="1919-04-09T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received April
                            10, 1919, 7.40 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your April 9, 6 p.m. This matter has received serious consideration. I have
                    [learned] through Abbott that the British, French think it far better to renew
                    the option, as they fear that otherwise the Japanese might use the interval
                    until the new consortium formed to commit (Republic?), at present dependent upon
                    them absolutely, to a currency arrangement favorable to Japan, particularly the
                    appointment of Sakatani.<anchor n="95" xml:id="d459-f1"/> As the intergroup
                    agreement expires June 19th next, Russia could then [be] automatically
                    eliminated and the option taken over immediately by the new consortium. Abbott
                    agrees with this and believes less trouble and risk to settle the matter in June
                    than now. Group representatives acting under instructions have asked for
                    renewal. In view of the above I beg to suggest reconsideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d459-f1" n="95" xml:id="d459-f1-content">
                <p>Baron Yoshiro Sakatani; see <ref target="#pg556">pp. 556</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
